>
> These numbers represent different entities: the 4 assets are systems/resources, while the 178 CBOM records represent cryptographic components identified across those assets.
>
> I can also break the 160 quantum-vulnerable components down by asset, algorithm, severity, application, or recommended migration path.

This is significantly better than simply returning:

> "No assets match that filter."

unless the user actually applied a filter that genuinely produces zero matching assets.

